Now let me read the protocol to understand the data format and expectations.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/protocol.md"
  }
}
```

Now I need to examine the actual data structure to understand what features and labels look like. Let me check one of the CSV files.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/patches/D0000/train.csv"
  }
}
```

I can see the data has 32 features (feat_0 to feat_31) and a label column with values 0-3 (foreground fraction bucket). The task is to train a segmentation baseline. Since we have tabular features and categorical labels (0-3), this appears to be a classification problem rather than pixel-wise segmentation. The "Dice" metric mentioned likely refers to some form of classification performance metric.

Let me check the test and validation files to understand the data splits better.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "head -n 5 data/patches/D0000/test.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this script to understand the data better.

